# Character System

The `Character` class represents playable characters.

The class contains the information required to describe a character and their basic combat statistics.

## Character Data

```text
Name
Title
Level

Current HP
Maximum HP

Current Ase
Maximum Ase

Attack
Defense
```

Conceptually, the class contains:

```cpp
std::string mName;
std::string mTitle;

int mLevel;

int mHP;
int mMaxHP;

int mAse;
int mMaxAse;

int mAttack;
int mDefense;
```

---

# Character Constructors

## Default Constructor

The default constructor creates an empty Character with safe starting values.

```text
Name:    Empty
Title:   Empty
Level:   1

HP:      0 / 0
Ase:     0 / 0

Attack:  0
Defense: 0
```

## Overloaded Constructor

The overloaded constructor allows a complete Character to be initialized.

Parameters:

```text
Name
Title
Maximum HP
Maximum Ase
Attack
Defense
```

New characters begin with full HP and full Ase.

Conceptually:

```text
Maximum HP = supplied Max HP
Current HP = Maximum HP

Maximum Ase = supplied Max Ase
Current Ase = Maximum Ase
```

---

# Character Getters

The Character class currently provides getters for its stored information.

```cpp
GetName()
GetTitle()
GetLevel()

GetHP()
GetMaxHP()

GetAse()
GetMaxAse()

GetAttack()
GetDefense()
```

The getter functions are marked `const` because retrieving character information should not modify the Character object.

---

# Character Setters

The Character class currently contains setters for HP and Ase.

```cpp
SetHP()
SetAse()
```

Both setters protect the Character from invalid resource values.

## HP Rules

```text
If HP < 0
    HP becomes 0

If HP > Maximum HP
    HP becomes Maximum HP

Otherwise
    HP becomes the supplied value
```

Therefore:

```text
0 <= HP <= Maximum HP
```

## Ase Rules

The same protection is used for Ase.

```text
If Ase < 0
    Ase becomes 0

If Ase > Maximum Ase
    Ase becomes Maximum Ase

Otherwise
    Ase becomes the supplied value
```

Therefore:

```text
0 <= Ase <= Maximum Ase
```

