# Enemy System

The `Enemy` class represents enemies encountered during gameplay.

The initial version deliberately keeps enemies simple.

Special attacks, status effects, elemental properties, and unique behaviors will be added in later development passes.

## Enemy Data

```text
Name
Current HP
Maximum HP
Attack
Defense
```

Conceptually:

```cpp
std::string mName;

int mHP;
int mMaxHP;

int mAttack;
int mDefense;
```

---

# Enemy Constructors

## Default Constructor

The default Enemy constructor initializes an empty Enemy.

```text
Name:    Empty
HP:      0 / 0
Attack:  0
Defense: 0
```

## Overloaded Constructor

The overloaded Enemy constructor receives:

```text
Name
Maximum HP
Attack
Defense
```

When an Enemy is created:

```text
Maximum HP = supplied Maximum HP
Current HP = Maximum HP
```

This causes every newly created enemy to begin at full health.

