# Planned Combat System

The next major system is the Combat class.

The first combat prototype will deliberately remain simple.

## v0.02 Combat Goals

```text
Start Battle
     |
     v
Display Battle Information
     |
     v
Player Chooses Action
     |
     v
Player Attacks Enemy
     |
     v
Enemy Attacks Player
     |
     v
Check HP
     |
     +---- Enemy HP <= 0 ----> Victory
     |
     +---- Player HP <= 0 ---> Defeat
     |
     v
Repeat Battle
```

Initial combat will use only basic attacks.

Advanced mechanics will be implemented only after the basic battle loop works correctly.

---

# Planned Reactive Combat

The long-term combat design uses a reactive turn-based system.

Enemies will eventually telegraph attacks through descriptive text.

The player will then choose how to respond.

Planned defensive actions include:

### Dodge

Safer defensive option focused on avoiding damage.

### Guard

Reduces incoming damage.

### Parry

Higher-risk defensive option.

A successful parry may interrupt an enemy attack or create a counterattack opportunity.

A failed parry may result in taking the full attack.

These systems are planned for a later version and are **not implemented in v0.01**.

